notes.text:
Albanian chooses the case by preposition:
- në shkollë with the accusative;
- nga shkolla with the nominative;
- para shkollës with the ablative.

Arabic has **one case after all prepositions: the genitive**.

If your prepositions govern different cases, Arabic is simpler:
- every preposition takes the genitive;
- the direction is in the preposition, never in the case.
